1791857406450325	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-n6g	{"description":"# Context & Background\nBob's follow-up spec to JARLDOM-SPEC.md v1, written 2026-10-12 (source file: ~/Downloads/JARLDOM-NEXT.md). Jarldom 0.1.x is released and live-tested (colony, villagers, rooms, the Thing, faith, ascension via pyre, ore claims, outposts, trade tiers, follow-the-jarl, weaver, leisure). This spec covers what comes next: eight Jarldom milestones (J1-J8) plus thirteen standalone mods that feed the colony (Bathhouse, Byre, Hounds/cats/hawks, Horses, Larder, Fields, Viking building kit, Shipyard, Tafl, Runecarver, Wounds and herbs, Raven post, Loom).\nItem numbers (#1..#85) in child bones point back to Bob's decision list. Priorities: P1 do first (urgency=urgent), P2 normal, P3 low (urgency=punt). \"Toggle\" = a server-authoritative setting to switch the feature off.\n\n# Ground rules (apply to EVERY child bone)\n- JARLDOM-SPEC.md section 3 still applies: read ~/repos/valheim-claude-tools/docs/modding-pitfalls.md first; prefix every name with the mod's (JarldomX, jarldom_x); server-authoritative settings; clean F6 reload; pure logic in Core/ testable classes linked into tests/<Mod>.Tests; a ClaudeTools command for every system; a README playtest checklist.\n- Standalone mods must be useful ON THEIR OWN. Each publishes a tiny `<Mod>.Api` static class (`int Version` + a few methods) that Jarldom finds by REFLECTION. No hard dependency in either direction (see foundations goal).\n- Spin-out rule (decided): only ITEMS AND CRAFTING leave Jarldom. Villagers and everything villagers do stay in Jarldom.\n- New items keep their prefab names FOREVER: renaming deletes them from players' saves.\n- Audio: use the game's own clips where they fit; anything new must be CC0 or our own recording, listed in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.\n- Release every change (memory rule): bump version, CHANGELOG/DESCRIPTION/README, dist + manifest, for the changed mod only. Raise Jarldom Plugin.DataVersion whenever ColonyRecord/VillagerState/soul/claim key formats change.\n- Network rule: nothing big on moving ZDOs (villager bodies); store on soul/record/saga ZDOs.\n\n# Decisions at a glance (from the spec)\nIn: 1,2,3,6(P3),8(capped),9,10(text only),11,12,13,15-19,20,21,22(P3),23,24(redesigned),25,26,27-31,32,33,34(toggle),35-38,39-40(P3),44-47,48-49(P3,toggle),51-55,59-71,73-78,80,81(P1),82-85.\nOptional (only if cheap): 7, 14, 50. Trial run first: 41-43 land spirits. Needs Bob's decision: 57 carts, 79 raven post. Use an existing mod: 72 seasons -> soft integration with shudnal's Seasons. Out: 4, 5, 56 (ore claims stay in Jarldom), 58, all of sections J and K.\n\n# Suggested order (section 4), wired as goal dependencies\n1 Bathhouse -> 2 J1 + J2 -> 3 Byre -> 4 Viking building kit -> 5 J3 -> 6 Loom spin-out -> 7 J4 -> 8 J5 -> 9 Shipyard -> J6 -> 10 Larder/Fields/Horses/Hounds/Tafl/Runecarver/Wounds as appetite allows -> 11 J8 picked up along the way -> 12 J7 land-spirit trial (after J6) -> 13 Raven post if approved.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every child goal closed or explicitly cut by Bob.\n- [ ] Each milestone's live acceptance test passed in Bob's Creative world and released.\n\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMoves Jarldom from a working colony sim to a living Norse society you come home to, while the standalone mods stay useful for players who never install Jarldom.","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga"],"size":"xl","title":"Jarldom: the next saga (spec JARLDOM-NEXT.md v1, 2026-10-12): J1-J8 additions + standalone feeder mods"}	blake3:YI-D-OtKf_tqDQSspE41ZjsYgYKvka3fL2yv5KCrPXQ
1791857501121049	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-r0a	{"description":"# Context & Background\nJARLDOM-NEXT.md section 5 lists five calls only Bob can make. Several bones are blocked on them (Raven post, Loom fallback, calendar default, Larder spoilage default, carts integration).\n# Goals\nGet each decision recorded on its child bone (comment + close), so the blocked work can start with no guessing.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nThe spec gives a recommendation for most; recording Bob's answer in bones keeps it durable across sessions and agents.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each child decision bone has Bob's answer as a comment and is closed.\n- [ ] Any bone that depended on the answer has been updated to match it.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nUnblocks the later milestones without rework.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","decision"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"s","title":"Next saga: open decisions for Bob (spec section 5)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:hTFx2PeDKpTGM2zmM2GHrnyOashV3AfVRodsJz6bXpU
1791857501192134	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-26k	{"description":"# Context & Background\nGround rule: each standalone mod publishes a tiny `<Mod>.Api` static class (`int Version` + a few methods) that Jarldom finds by reflection; no hard dependency either way. Today only Omens/Api.cs (GetFate/AddFate) and Shieldwall/Api.cs (IsSiegeAt/CallOff/StoneAt) exist, and Jarldom's Compat/Compat.cs calls them ad hoc. The next saga adds ~15 more Api consumers (Wayfinder, GraveGoods, Bathhouse, Byre, Hounds, Horses, Shipyard, Runecarver, Tafl, Wounds, Loom, Seasons, BountyBoard, Arena, Golf).\n# Goals\nOne shared, tested pattern for publishing and consuming Apis, so each integration bone is a few lines rather than a new reflection hack.\n# Reasoning/Justification\nReflection keeps mods independently installable (Bob's rule) and survives version skew via `Version`. A shared helper avoids 15 copies of fragile MethodInfo lookups and handles \"mod present but older Api\" uniformly.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Child tasks done; at least Omens and Shieldwall consumed through the new helper with no behaviour change.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEvery J8 connection and every standalone-mod \"Jarldom API\" milestone builds on this.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","foundations","integration"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"m","title":"Next saga: shared foundations (Api convention + reflection lookup + upstream Api additions)","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:_K8XR5wG0I0Hq0-LY2leXtg6iXTV81gL39fCVURSwpo
1791857501265455	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3je	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.1. The colony works but feels silent and static. J1 is cheap, mostly presentation, and gives the biggest jump in how alive it feels, so it is done first (with J2), right after the Bathhouse.\nItems: #1 soundscape, #2 quiet when miserable, #3 desire paths (toggle), #6 work you can see (P3), #7 watch lamp (optional), #8 personal corners (capped), #9 greetings, #10 work songs (text only), #11 northern lights, #12 village dogs.\n# Goals\nHear the colony working; see its paths form; have villagers greet you, sing at work, gaze at the aurora, and keep dogs that warn of raids.\n# Acceptance Criteria (spec)\n- [ ] Stand in the hall at dusk with 8 villagers: the noise is clearly there; push mood below -40 and it goes quiet.\n- [ ] Over 3 in-game days a path appears between the longhouse and the woodlot and nowhere random.\n- [ ] A villager hangs their first trophy on your stand.\n- [ ] A wolf barks before a raid shows up on screen.\n- [ ] Released (version bump, changelog, dist).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nThe \"living colony\" feel is the core promise of Jarldom; everything later (festivals, verse, afterlife) reads better when the place already sounds and looks inhabited.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j1","p1"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"J1: A living colony (P1) - soundscape, desire paths, greetings, work songs, aurora, village dogs","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:zeNfmUlNVeyThwflyPaEjlTvsadutigmfuLgRmkA330
1791857501340538	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-11e	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.2. Coming home should feel like an event: the beacon is lit, people meet you at the dock, you have a byname earned from your deeds, eating and sleeping among villagers matter, and the skald turns the day into verse.\nItems: #13 beacon, #15 player bynames, #16 co-jarls compared, #17 eating in the hall, #18 sleeping among them, #19 skald's verse, #14 laying trophies at the high seat (optional).\n# Acceptance Criteria (spec)\n- [ ] Sail home at night: the beacon is lit before you land, and villagers are at the dock.\n- [ ] After a boss kill your byname changes and the next night's verse names the boss.\n- [ ] Released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTies the player's adventures to the colony; the byname tally and verse system are reused by J3 (memorial), J4 (festivals), J5 (requests), J8 (Arena/Tafl champions).\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j2","p1"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"l","title":"J2: The jarl's return (P1) - beacon, bynames, hall meals, sleeping among them, skald's verse","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:fE3l0-fdyAC3X6X3H3Gm-U6OBuiLQ-CZIBp8KcKwO50
1791857501414994	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3k3	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.3. Ascension exists today via the funeral pyre (Colony/Behaviours.cs) and souls carry worth; lost souls rise as draugr. J3 deepens death and memory.\nItems: #20 funeral ship, #21 Valkyrie flyover, #22 raven on the runestone (P3), #23 they answer back, #24 the Dimming (redesigned), #25 memorial wall, #26 laying the lost to rest.\n# Acceptance Criteria (spec)\n- [ ] Take one villager from arrival to the funeral ship; rewards apply once even with F6 mid-ceremony.\n- [ ] A Dimmed villager shows a request in their panel, and completing it clears the Dimming.\n- [ ] Kill and bury a lost soul: the memorial updates and grief ends.\n- [ ] Released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nDeath and remembrance are the heart of the Norse framing (worth, Valhalla, Hel); this gives ascension a spectacle and gives stagnating souls a gentle, recoverable pressure.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j3","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"J3: The afterlife (P2) - funeral ship, Valkyrie, einherjar, the Dimming, memorial wall, the lost laid to rest"}	blake3:oj0KrRkNuH2LMlvcIbVVdl_msoxyPpv7a6Wp9eL8rpk
1791857501487851	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-12d	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.4. No calendar or festivals exist in code yet (only feasts and the Thing). #27 calendar, #72 shudnal's Seasons soft integration (do NOT build seasons ourselves), #28-31 four festivals, each with preparation (goods to the hall in the 2 days before), the event (dusk to dawn) and a blessing lasting until the next festival, scaled by preparation; skipping one gives a small neglect penalty.\nDefault year: 40 in-game days, four 10-day seasons (open decision 4 - confirm with Bob).\n# Acceptance Criteria (spec)\n- [ ] A full colony year in test (`jarldom time`): each festival announces its preparation, runs, and applies and removes its blessing.\n- [ ] With Seasons installed, the dates follow its seasons.\n- [ ] Released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGives the colony a rhythm and long-term goals; the calendar is reused by J3 anniversaries (#22), J6 shielings (summer half-year), Fields crops, Horses races.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j4","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"l","title":"J4: The Norse year (P2) - colony calendar, Seasons soft integration, Yule / Midsummer / Winter Nights / Sigrblot"}	blake3:nPHEu6qigs-wqG-QExia0MUuDTl5JH346rcTkS5a2xI
1791857501561220	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1d4	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.5. The colony should send the player out into the world. Items: #32 villager requests, #33 BountyBoard contracts, #34 true legends (toggle), #35 expectations rise, #36 relics for temples, #37 the land wears thin, #38 Odin the Wanderer (Saga renown part), #39 colony map table (P3), #40 edge of the map (P3).\n# Acceptance Criteria (spec)\n- [ ] With 6 villagers, at least 4 kinds of request appear over 5 days, all doable.\n- [ ] A legend leads to a real crypt.\n- [ ] A temple can't reach grade A without its relic.\n- [ ] Renown shows a Saga part that rises when you enter a new biome.\n- [ ] Released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTurns the colony from a base you return to into a source of adventures; requests also power the Dimming's way back (#24) and raven/BountyBoard integrations.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j5","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"J5: Reasons to roam (P2) - villager requests, BountyBoard, true legends, rising expectations, relics, worn land, Saga renown"}	blake3:IyYwI-DogsNyyhMlovP980w6FxWk7C7-qHUJLNEi1go
1791857501633734	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-bvx	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.6. Builds on follow-the-jarl (Villager/Follow.cs), outposts (World/Outposts.cs), ore claims, trade tiers. Items: #53 expeditions (P1 within J6), #52 scattered reborn, #46 shipwright, #45 island jarldoms, #44 shielings, #47 Great Works, #51 legends from runestones, #54 Dvergr trade relations, #48-49 roads that grow (P3, toggle, last), #50 reclaim ruins (optional).\n# Acceptance Criteria (spec)\n- [ ] Lead a 4-person expedition by karve to a new island, make camp, upgrade it to an outpost.\n- [ ] Rescue a scattered soul.\n- [ ] The shipwright builds a karve from stockpiles.\n- [ ] Complete one Great Work and see its bonus applied.\n- [ ] Released.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nExtends the colony's reach across the map, making ships, outposts and exploration part of colony life.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j6","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"J6: Expeditions and reach (P2) - expeditions, scattered reborn, shipwright, islands, shielings, Great Works, Dvergr, roads"}	blake3:cmW3oafH3tiDv__OnF2PwHw2Zy4tjUBWIMQocrEhIbs
1791857501708301	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1fn	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.7. Bob is unsure about the complexity, so this is a time-boxed 2-day trial with an explicit go/no-go, not a feature commitment. It plugs into claims and outposts, so it comes after J6.\n# Smallest version worth testing\nRegions = 64 m zones grouped into 512 m cells (pure arithmetic, nothing saved until claimed). One spirit stone per cell at an existing game location (standing stone, runestone, landmark) chosen by seed. Win it over with one biome-chosen task: offering (biome food), clear threats (kill N hostiles within 60 m), or vigil (stand there one night). Effects (only two): villagers may work and claim ore there; raids starting in a claimed cell are -25%. Dragon prow (#43) only if go.\n# Go / no-go\nGo if claiming feels like a small adventure and changes where you send people. No-go: cut #42-43, keep spirit stones only as a legend source for #34.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Trial built behind a setting, played by Bob, decision recorded as a comment; follow-up bones created or cut.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nTests whether territory can have personality without a heavy new system.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j7","trial"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"m","title":"J7: Land spirits - 2-day TRIAL RUN with go/no-go (#41-43)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:2nsfjqCyN-PFrPIaPOiFjDgUBuBrMOm2igMs-YPjVhE
1791857501780995	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1gf	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 2.8: #82 GraveGoods, #83 Arena, #84 Shieldwall, #85 Golf. Picked up along the way whenever each of those mods is touched (spec section 4 item 11), so this goal is not gated behind the main chain.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each connection works with the other mod installed and does nothing (no errors) without it.\n- [ ] Released on both sides when an Api changes.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nMakes Bob's mod collection feel like one world.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["jarldom","next-saga","j8","p2","integration"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"m","title":"J8: Connections to Bob's other mods (P2) - GraveGoods, Arena, Shieldwall, Golf"}	blake3:0RxWnvdxZhPITowbS__70eZxZgcofniVGWUB33aUFAA
1791857501851866	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-33h	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.1, first in the build order: small, standalone, P1. A Jarldom petition already asks to \"Build a sauna\"; nothing exists in code yet.\nAlone: buildable sauna stove, bench, water bucket (throw water on the stones for steam). Sit in a sauna room (roofed, enclosed, stove + bench) for 60 s -> Bathed buff (comfort +2, Rested +10 min, stamina regen +10%, cold resistance, cures Wet). An outdoor cold plunge (a tub, or a dip in water) right after -> Invigorated (+5% move speed, +10% stamina, 10 min). Shared bathing (2+ players) lengthens it.\nJarldom: a Bathhouse room type (Beauty + Rested); villagers bathe after work (mood +, Social +); answers the sauna petition.\nMilestones: B1 pieces + buff + room check, B2 cold plunge + shared bathing, B3 Jarldom API (`Bathhouse.Api.IsSauna(pos)`).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Works with no Jarldom installed; with Jarldom, villagers bathe and the petition is satisfied.\n- [ ] Published as its own mod in dist/manifest.json.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nA quick, self-contained win that adds a Norse daily-life ritual and a new Jarldom room type.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["bathhouse","next-saga","standalone","p1"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"l","title":"Bathhouse (Badstofa) standalone mod (#81, P1): sauna, cold plunge, Jarldom bathhouse room","urgency":"urgent"}	blake3:D2s_gEDFZC2fg6K5buKmMYGG_PZsicIE1rjcc7IA4VA
1791857501925642	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-24c	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.2, third in the build order. Alone: sheep (shear -> wool), goats (milk; climb steep slopes), cattle (milk, hides, pull a plow if Fields is installed), geese (eggs, feathers; chase strangers), pigs (bred from tamed boars; truffles in the Black Forest). Wild herds to tame in the right biomes; breeding with the game's procreation; feeding troughs; stall barn piece set; milk pail and shears.\nJarldom: herder and dairymaid work (a Herder + Pasture zone exists already), wool -> the weaver, dairy -> the cook, a Byre room type (stalls + trough + roof) whose warmth adds +1 comfort to a longhouse sharing a wall with it.\nMilestones: S1 sheep + goats + shearing/milking + troughs, S2 cattle + geese + pigs, S3 barn set + Jarldom API.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All milestones shipped; useful alone; Jarldom integration via Byre.Api.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFeeds the weaver and cook, gives herders real work, supplies Fields (manure, plow) and Larder (dairy).\n","kind":"goal","labels":["byre","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Byre (livestock) standalone mod (#59, #60): sheep, goats, cattle, geese, pigs, barn set"}	blake3:ek5yfrmg-5Riv-ivOcPg0MBIqGzXI7IH8F6LQWeCGfU
1791857502003087	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-10n	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.3 (\"as appetite allows\"). Hounds: raise a tamed wolf pup into a herding dog (keeps livestock together, brings strays home) or a war hound (follows, fights, tracks wounded game), whistle commands. Cats: tame a wild Meadows cat; near food storage they stop a pests loss (only if Larder spoilage is on; otherwise comfort +1 and purr). Falconry: catch a young hawk in the Mountains (BirdTrap-style bait trap if present), train it, fly it at birds/small game, it returns with the kill.\nJarldom: village dogs (#12) use trained hounds; herders get herding dogs; hunters a hawk; cats protect the granary.\nMilestones: H1 hounds, H2 cats, H3 falconry.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped and useful alone; Hounds.Api consumed by Jarldom #12.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAnimal companions for players and better village dogs for Jarldom.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["hounds","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Hounds, cats and hawks standalone mod (#63, #64, #65)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:y8-osT6XFE0KhBwSVqHI7rucf5VaaQGEdM9OfFzMpC4
1791857502082178	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1k8	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.4. Wild herds in Meadows and Plains; catch with a rope, break in by riding (it bucks, you hold on with stamina); saddles in tiers; stamina and speed; breeding with inherited speed and stamina; brushing for a bond bonus. Teams: harness to a cart (PassengerCart through its API, or the game's cart) or to a plow (Fields).\nJarldom: carters and scouts ride; plowed fields yield more; horse races at Midsummer.\nMilestones: R1 taming + riding + saddle, R2 breeding + traits, R3 harness (cart, plow) + Jarldom API.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped and useful alone; Horses.Api consumed by Jarldom.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nOverland transport and farming power; colour for Midsummer.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["horses","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Horses standalone mod (#61, #62): taming, riding, saddles, breeding, harness","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:HkqsRctmZv2CJrgwESnGoNJ39ePqP9YcjVuj70AtNkQ
1791857502157985	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3ci	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.5. Spoilage (toggle, OFF by default - open decision 5): raw food spoils over days, slower in cold or roofed storage; preserved food never does. Smokehouse (meat, fish), salting barrel, stockfish drying racks (fish dries outdoors over days), root cellar (room type that slows spoilage), dairy (butter churn, cheese press, skyr), bread oven (rye and barley breads). New mid-tier preserved foods for long voyages.\nJarldom: cooks preserve food; expedition supplies; winter stores; food variety for mood.\nMilestones: L1 preserved foods + smokehouse + racks, L2 dairy + oven, L3 spoilage (toggle) + root cellar.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped; spoilage off by default unless Bob decides otherwise.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFood depth for voyages and expeditions (J6), cats (H2), cooks.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["larder","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Larder standalone mod (#66, #67, #68): preserved foods, smokehouse, dairy, oven, optional spoilage","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:6R2hEyZI9NCWlTDKkQHOTFm0eHN2vLw9BHyn_6JbRwc
1791857502230598	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2q8	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.6. New crops (rye, peas, cabbage, leeks, angelica, hops), each with a biome and season (with Seasons installed); soil fertility per tilled patch, drained by harvest and restored by fallow, manure (Byre) or rotation (legumes); a plow (horse or ox team) tilling a strip; scarecrows; apple trees (years to bear); Idunn's apples as a rare late-game graft with a long, strong regen buff. Farmhand compatibility (row planting and harvest work with the new crops - Farmhand is Bob's own mod in mods/Farmhand).\nJarldom: farmers rotate crops; food variety; #37 worn-land pressure uses real soil numbers.\nMilestones: F1 crops, F2 fertility + rotation + plow, F3 orchards + Idunn's apples.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped and useful alone; Farmhand works with the new crops.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nFarming depth for players and Jarldom's farmers; ingredients for Larder breads (rye, barley).\n","kind":"goal","labels":["fields","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Fields and orchards standalone mod (#69, #70, #71): new crops, fertility, plow, orchards, Idunn's apples","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:X4ZxoeLEca75qNzjpUeVsTTpLpZyVqj7i1nYP08u_HY
1791857502303327	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3ik	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.7, fourth in the build order (helps Hallwright and room grades at once). Turf roofs (sod on birch bark, insulating: +comfort under it), stave-church pieces (staves, carved portals, shingle roofs), wattle fences and walls, wall benches (sleep on them: bed-tier comfort), smoke-hole roof pieces (vent a hearth with no chimney), granary on stilts, market stalls, shutters, carved door frames, runic lintels. All with proper snap points and support values.\nHallwright (mods/BuildShapes): add the kit to its material styles (turf longhouse, stave-church temple). Jarldom: more pieces for room grades; wall benches as longhouse beds.\nMilestones: K1 turf roofs + wall benches + smoke-hole, K2 stave-church set, K3 market + granary + details, K4 Hallwright styles.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped; pieces snap and carry load correctly; Hallwright styles use them.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nAuthentic Norse architecture for every player; better rooms for Jarldom.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["buildkit","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Viking building kit standalone mod (#73): turf roofs, wall benches, smoke-hole, stave church, market, Hallwright styles"}	blake3:cJer9oGDsjY-Dj_58qIo5vMNh6ePaiWpH9KaW9DB2u4
1791857502382496	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2n2	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.8, built just before J6. Slipway: ships built in visible stages (keel -> ribs -> strakes -> deck -> mast), each stage paid in full (pitfall: no partial-payment item loss), buildable by several players. Boathouse (naust) protects moored ships from wear. Repairs at the slipway. New hulls: faering (fast little rowboat) and knarr (wide cargo ship, holds far more than the longship, slower, sails well in strong wind). \"The knarr is the sea answer to 'no ore through portals.'\"\nJarldom: the shipwright profession builds them; island jarldoms and trade by sea run on knarrs. Wayfinder: ship names and fittings apply to the new hulls.\nMilestones: N1 slipway + staged building + faering, N2 knarr, N3 boathouse + repairs + Jarldom API.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped and useful alone; Shipyard.Api consumed by the J6 shipwright.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nSea logistics for J6 (islands, trade, shipwright) and a satisfying ship-building activity alone.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["shipyard","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Shipyard (Naust) standalone mod (#74, #75): slipway staged builds, faering, knarr, boathouse"}	blake3:IXDjKW6gqW7XxzEzJjIndkd5QiRolIZNtuapNFo_mvs
1791857502461356	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-350	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.9. Tafl board table piece: playable hnefatafl (11x11, standard rules), PvP or vs AI (search depth by difficulty); dice (a cup, betting in coins); knattleikr (ball and two bats on a marked field, simple rules, physics ball). Jarldom already has leisure \"tafl\" as an idle activity (Villager/Leisure.cs) without a real game.\nJarldom: villagers play tafl in the hall evenings (simulated games, pieces moving); a tafl champion byname; challenge a villager to a real game; dice gambling moodlet.\nMilestones: T1 hnefatafl PvP, T2 AI, T3 dice + knattleikr, T4 Jarldom API.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped; rules engine fully unit-tested.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nEvening culture for players and villagers.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["tafl","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Tafl and games standalone mod (#76, #77): hnefatafl board + AI, dice, knattleikr","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:SyTNjINs45HJmYYLrbIkyWysprt2H6X8tnjWMA57R6s
1791857502534613	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-21n	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.10. Carve runestones with your own text, transliterated to Younger Futhark (long-branch) with a documented English -> Old Norse SOUND mapping (no translation), carved in a band along a serpent outline; choose stone shape and paint colours; hover shows the English. Also shields, door lintels, memorial stones.\nJarldom: memorial wall (#25), milestones (#48), gravestones and chronicle stones render in runes.\nMilestones: C1 transliteration (pure-logic tests) + one stone, C2 serpent band rendering + shapes + paint, C3 Jarldom API.\nPrior art: Jarldom 0.1.18 carves real runes into meshes via Blender (mods/Jarldom/Models/carve/carve.py); runtime text needs a different approach (decal/texture or generated mesh).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped; transliteration fully unit-tested.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nPersonal, permanent marks in the world; runic rendering for Jarldom memorials.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["runecarver","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"l","title":"Runecarver standalone mod (#78): Younger Futhark runestones, shields, lintels, memorials","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:ouCckmL_1e_KLUm5NQJlLVgK3BWmFVQiOLoPeB0aVLw
1791857502615083	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-4nf	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.11. Toggle per wound type: bleeding (slashes; bandage stops it), broken bones (big falls or troll hits; slower until splinted, then heals over time), infection (untreated wounds in the swamp; fever debuff; herbs cure it). Herb garden (yarrow, angelica, plantain) and a mortar for poultices and bandages.\nJarldom: healer and healer's house get real work (a Healer HealTask exists already); injured villagers need treatment; expeditions want a medic.\nMilestones: W1 bleeding + bandages, W2 bones + splints, W3 infection + herbs + garden, W4 Jarldom API.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped with per-type toggles; useful alone.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nGives combat consequences and the healer profession purpose.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["wounds","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"xl","title":"Wounds and herbs standalone mod (#80): bleeding, broken bones, infection, herb garden, poultices","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:6xf1VU-T_Dz_vonXEKyq0XzSIxhxVK8Nsunczpa4Wec
1791857502690508	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2jw	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.12. A raven roost piece: write a short message (+ up to one stack of a light item, <= 10 kg) to any player, roost or outpost you know. The raven flies the real distance in game time (~150 m/min), visible in flight; on arrival a sound at the roost, a pin, and the item+message in the roost's slot; if the recipient is offline it waits at their home roost. Hazards: over Mountains hawks may take it (item lost, raven returns); storms make it land and wait; trained ravens are faster and safer. Ravens you raise have a name, delivery count and byname. Hugin's cousins: send to an unexplored pin, it flies there and back and reveals a strip of map.\nJarldom: outposts send daily reports; expedition villagers send news; requests (#32) can arrive by raven.\nOverlap: Delivery's courier already brings items to you. Raven post is player-to-player and base-to-base; keep distinct or fold into Delivery as a second courier type.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Bob's decision recorded; if \"build\" or \"fold\", child bones created from this description; if \"drop\", close as cut.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLong-distance communication between players and outposts.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["ravenpost","next-saga","standalone","decision"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"l","title":"Raven post (#79) - PROPOSAL, blocked on Bob's decision (build / fold into Delivery / drop)","urgency":"punt"}	blake3:9wYmtUnr3axywEHiMM5a4rWItiR02dKWgQu9I0fmX2c
1791857502766727	claude-jarldom	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3kf	{"description":"# Context & Background\nSpec section 3.13 and the spin-out rule (only items and crafting leave Jarldom). Today Villager/Weaving.cs makes Hildir's tunics/dresses/caps as colony-only recipes and flax grows in colony fields.\nMoves out: flax processing, spinning wheel use, the loom, dyes (berries, bark), tunics/dresses/caps craftable by players; clothing slots and warmth as Jarldom has them now.\nStays in Jarldom: weaver profession and AI, villager outfits, Hildir purchases by traders.\nSave safety: moved prefabs KEEP their current Jarldom* names (allowed exception to the naming rule, noted in code). Loom registers them; Jarldom stops registering them when Loom is present.\nOpen question (decision bone): without Loom, does Jarldom (a) keep registering them itself, or (b) require Loom for clothes and hide the weaver? Recommendation: (a) for one release with a deprecation note, then (b).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No player loses a clothing item in any install/uninstall order (Loom only, Jarldom only, both, upgrade from old Jarldom).\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nLets non-Jarldom players weave and dress; keeps Jarldom focused on villagers.\n","kind":"goal","labels":["loom","jarldom","next-saga","standalone","p2"],"parent":"bn-n6g","size":"l","title":"Loom spin-out (#55): move clothing items and crafting out of Jarldom into a standalone Loom mod"}	blake3:XJ1Hr_u8L8Qxfx-MnjvO8R7zo-9lAbQjkmGI8kjO1Mg
