1792298242499023	claude-bathhouse	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-3kf	{"field":"title","value":"Homespun standalone mod (#55, grown): fibre to cloth to garments - retting, spinning, warp-weighted loom, real dyeing, sewing, garments with a purpose; Jarldom runs the chain"}	blake3:5iB-zDWizZCXY8T-7Ra4bz8BTm6O1P3fZyFYx0kRoqg
1792298242503850	claude-bathhouse	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-3kf	{"field":"description","value":"# Context & Background\nWas 'Loom spin-out' (move Jarldom's colony-only weaving out). Renamed and re-scoped with Bob on 2026-10-18 after finding the spin-out bought little: Jarldom's clothes are the game's own Hildir items (ArmorTunic*/ArmorDress*/HelmetHat*) and LinenThread, it registers no clothing prefabs, so there was no save-safety problem and nothing worth moving. Vanilla garment making is only flax -> spinning wheel -> linen thread as an armour ingredient; no loom, no cloth, no sewing, no dye (Hildir's clothes are bought, one item per colour).\nName: Homespun (cloth spun and woven at home); GUID cx.bob.homespun. No Thunderstore mod by that name (checked 2026-10-18). Stonaar-DyeYourGear exists (recolouring): look at how it tints before H2.\n\n# The mod\n- Fibre: flax (Plains) with retting (soak in water some days) then breaking/combing; wool (lox, or sheep from Byre - see the fibre decision bone); maybe nettle fibre as an early-game cloth (needs a new plant).\n- Spinning: a drop spindle hand tool (anywhere, slow) and the game's spinning wheel (fast, at home).\n- Weaving: a warp-weighted loom (standing loom with stone weights): thread -> bolts of linen, wool, vadmal (coarse homespun, once money); tablet-woven bands for trim.\n- Dyeing (H2): a dye vat really recolours cloth and garments (woad/blueberries blue, madder/raspberries red, weld/dandelion yellow, lichen purple as a luxury). Colour kept in the item's custom data and shown on worn gear for everyone (tint the worn mesh; the game never recolours gear, so this is the hard part).\n- Sewing: a sewing table makes linen undertunics, wool tunics/dresses/trousers, hooded cloaks, nalbinding socks and mittens; Hildir's clothes craftable too.\n- Garments with a purpose (H3): light on armour; wool keeps out cold (cross the Mountains early in a heavy cloak), fulled/oiled wool sheds rain, fine dyed clothes give comfort/rested. A clothing layer under armour is the full version (new slot; Bathhouse already adds gear slots) - decision bone.\n- Beyond clothes (H3): wool sails (Shipyard knarr; Wayfinder sail colour/pattern), hall tapestries (Oseberg), banners.\n\n# Milestones\nH1 fibre -> cloth -> sewn garments; H2 real dyeing (MP); H3 garment effects, sails, tapestries, Api.\n\n# Jarldom (soft integration via the Api convention; children labelled jarldom)\nThe weaver runs the real chain (spinner/weaver/dyer on the real stations, retting pools, looms in the longhouse); colony colours chosen by the jarl, ranks in finer cloth and trim (#35); wool for cold/winter or a cold moodlet; vadmal as Thing fines and a trade good; sails for the shipwright's knarrs; tapestries/banners in room grades and feast mood; festival clothes. Without Homespun, Jarldom's weaver keeps today's Weaving.cs.\n\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Each milestone shipped and useful alone, with or without Jarldom.\n- [ ] No player loses an item in any install/uninstall order (Homespun only, Jarldom only, both, remove Homespun).\n- [ ] Dyed colours seen by a second client.\n- [ ] Jarldom's weaver runs the chain when Homespun is installed.\n# How This Serves Project Goals\nA satisfying craft for any player, and real cloth for the colony: clothes, colours, money, sails.\n# Risks\nRecolouring worn gear in MP; wool source (lox or Byre); new models via the bake pipeline (docs/model-baking.md); a clothing under-layer slot."}	blake3:FoQz-jESLAEFOt7IWC_W6DhNuSChEap6MNiNdrL9mEQ
