1792354679305645	claude-bathhouse	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-uvx0	{"description":"# Context\nBob 2026-10-18, screenshot of Creative's map: dozens of white pins 'A burial chamber (a legend)', 'A fallen stone tower (a legend)', 'A troll's cave (a legend)', 'A wrecked ship (a legend)' around Shithole, labels overlapping into an unreadable mass. Bob: 'the system where rumors turn to points on the map might be a bit too much. we should probably limit them'.\n# Cause\nWorld/TrueLegends.cs: with a jarl in the great hall, a legend is told every TellEvery = 240 real s; the 3rd telling pins it (TrueLegend.HeardForPin) and a new legend starts. So about one pin per 12 min of a jarl standing in the hall, with no cap, no expiry and no removal once visited. Bob idles in the hall a lot.\n# Ideas (pick with Bob or take sensible defaults)\n- Cap pins alive at once (e.g. 3-5 per colony); no new legend starts while the cap is reached.\n- Slow it down: tellings once per in-game evening/feast, not every 4 min; a legend takes days to pin.\n- Remove a legend pin once the place is visited/cleared (player within ~30 m, or the location's dungeon cleared), or after N days.\n- Shorter labels ('Troll cave?' or just the kind) so they don't overlap; maybe one pin icon without text.\n- Clean-up for existing saves: drop surplus legend pins (they're tracked in player custom data jarldom_legendpins) keeping the nearest few.\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Never more than the cap of legend pins on a jarl's map; old excess pins removed once.\n- [ ] Visited legends drop off the map.\n- [ ] A long idle in the hall doesn't add pins faster than the cap allows.","kind":"bug","labels":["jarldom","j5","legends"],"title":"Jarldom: limit true-legend map pins (Bob: 'might be a bit too much') - dozens of '(a legend)' pins crowd the map"}	blake3:_oxuSlq6-00iOXtOvxvszb_J2tCeyBtOKG2hNWXVvFc
