1792357780954286	claude-bathhouse	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1kmy	{"description":"# Context\nBob 2026-10-18, screenshot: a seated villager (hooded, blue tunic) in sit_fold_arms. The elbows are pulled in too close to the body: the forearms cross low and tight, pressed into the belly and side, so it doesn't read as relaxed folded arms. Bob: 'the cross-arms-while-sitting pose in bob's animations puts the elbows too close in'.\n# Where\nmods/BobsAnimations/Authoring/seated.py fold_arms(c) (Blender IK authoring, see the bobs-animations-design and blender-anim-pipeline memories), exported to Clips/sit_fold_arms.json.gz.\n# Fix\nMove the elbow targets / IK poles outward (elbows out to the sides, a little forward of the ribs), raise the folded forearms a bit to chest height, hands tucked by the opposite upper arm. Check from the front and the side at seat height that the forearms don't clip into the torso or each other, on both a slim and a broad villager body; check it still loops cleanly (keyframes [1, 45]).\n# Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Elbows sit clearly out from the body; folded arms read naturally from the front.\n- [ ] No clipping into the chest/belly; loop seamless.\n- [ ] Released (Bob's Animations version bump, dist).","kind":"bug","labels":["bobs-animations","animation"],"title":"Bob's Animations: sit_fold_arms puts the elbows too close in (forearms jammed against the body, folded arms read wrong)"}	blake3:KT05_J-tAk3MlSjnFxUlANNOvd3tuFoDer6toaFonS8
1792360939638817	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2tkg	{"description":"Bob 2026-10-18: with Hand (180,0,90) (released 0.1.1) the pail still wants a 90° turn about its vertical axis. A turn about its own y axis brings back (-90,90,0), which he rejected (fist on the rim), so the pail is probably tilted in the hand: try a turn about the line down from the fist. Tune live with byre grip ByreMilkPail ex ey ez while Bob holds it still, then save in mods/Byre/Items.cs Hand. Milking itself works (Bob, 2026-10-18).","kind":"bug","labels":["byre","needs-player"],"title":"Byre: milk pail still needs a 90° turn about its vertical axis in the hand"}	blake3:5BWWklnf2jCFM0NsegEyCUSFiMixcoO4UariKITrHKQ
