1792456723620203	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-333b	{"description":"Shipyard 0.3.0. A knarr is afloat? No: launch one from the boatyard slipway (344, 1182; lay knarr with Shift+E to pick the hull, or 'yard at 344 1182 lay knarr' + pay). Take the helm: Half and Full should set the sail (it unfurls from the yard), Stop furls it. Compare her speed with the longship in light wind and in a gale (she should be slower in light airs, faster in strong wind). Check her steering and heel when turning, the four seats on the sea chests, both ladders from the water into the hold, the 8x6 hold. Name her at the helm (Shift+E, Wayfinder). Look over the knarr's models at each stage and the naust's. Build a naust by hand at a shore and moor a ship inside: it should take no wear from the shore. Mend a damaged ship with the hammer near a slipway. Note: in this world FeedFromChests burns stored resin in torches, so a colony shipwright may run short.","kind":"task","labels":["needs-player"],"title":"Shipyard: sail the knarr, use the naust by hand (needs Bob)"}	blake3:5a8k95ejXH14PVQW0e42xgXS3LnkO5YLrjhUAvz5SMQ
1792457826804018	claude	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-333b	{"field":"title","value":"Shipyard: handle the knarr and use the naust by hand (needs Bob)"}	blake3:h7NLZ2bynPiqTWdWGGv_stAvHzrOYKBm560yqgA2jCU
1792457826817072	claude	itc:AQ		item.update	bn-333b	{"field":"description","value":"Shipyard 0.3.1. Measured already (Claude took the helm with the test tools, wind astern at Full): knarr 3.7 m/s vs longship 5.9 in light wind (0.2), 8.2 vs 9.1 in a gale (0.9); the sail sets half and full and furls at Stop. Still for Bob: launch one from the boatyard slipway (344, 1182) by hand (Shift+E picks the hull), and judge how she handles: steering, turning heel, sailing across the wind, whether the speeds feel right. Try the four seats on the sea chests, both ladders from the water into the hold, the 8x6 hold. Name her at the helm (Shift+E, Wayfinder). Look over the knarr's models at each stage, and the naust's. Build a naust by hand at a shore and moor a ship inside (no wear from the shore). Mend a damaged ship with the hammer near a slipway. Note: FeedFromChests burns stored resin in torches, so a colony shipwright may run short."}	blake3:M5ZMv6O6v4gn-0v1SmQQKpQjGWJAKwnnTUg6ZSVBILw
1792457826928569	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-ly9l	{"description":"Found 2026-10-19 while clearing test boats: Bob's saved fleet (player data bob_wayfinder_ships:<world>) lists Sea Stallion as 1|136596 at (384.1, 1128.8), and a Karve stands there, but ZDOMan.GetZDO(that id) returned null on the host. Suspected: ZDO ids are given afresh when a world loads, so ids saved in the fleet don't survive a restart. If so, Ships.Fleet's 'where she lay, she is not' check would tell Bob his ship is gone (and drop its pin) when he comes within 40 m of her in a loaded zone. Not yet checked: whether that message really fires near the karve, and whether being aboard again re-adds her under the new id. A fix might match by position and prefab instead of id (or store a ZDO-saved key of our own on the ship). Not changed: only reported.","kind":"bug","title":"Wayfinder: saved fleet ids go stale (a ship looked up by id isn't found)"}	blake3:74h_Ls83ZVzso0FiHIhN0BocprU6QJ9GzQSXbh2a8SU
1792459250093048	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-22pg	{"body":"Built in maw workspace jarlcloth, commit 5d0ad21 (not merged, not live-tested). Colours chosen in the Hall tab (1-2 of Homespun.Api.Dyes, kept as colony flags colour:1/colour:2, CropChoice-hashed: no save change); action 'colours', test 'jarldom colours [blue red|off]'. Weaver DyeTask (Villager/Dyeing.cs): stockpiles' plain garments (up to 4) + dyestuff (10 kept back) into an empty Homespun_DyeVat, back after steeping to take dyed ones out to the stores; says when the stores lack dyestuff (idle line too). Villagers swap plain clothes for the colours (OutfitTask 'colours'), sworn-to-a-jarl then Worth then oldest first (Jarldom has no villager ranks: that's the standing used). Bolts are never dyed (would block the sewing recipes). Test: jarldom dye [weaver]."}	blake3:TeKQG3Kt2oSoFSM3aHnz1I7VwM57p6mmYKB8WFDNdgA
1792459250113510	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2mr1	{"body":"Built in maw workspace jarlcloth, commit 5d0ad21 (not live-tested). Feast: 2+ tapestries in the great hall -> 'feasthung' moodlet (+26, 60h) instead of 'feast' (+20, 48h), saga line. Festival clothes: on a festival's day Gear.Maintain wears the finest (dyed, colony colours highest) before armour, guards excepted; 'finery' +5 moodlet held while so; next day back to the sturdiest. A finer garment than what's worn is kept in the bag (not Spare) for festivals. No lending from the stores. Test: jarldom finery on|off."}	blake3:nJywn-9eGKdL-HhBQl7ObIpD1hqvY4FmyogHBibWJAc
1792459250131482	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-15j9	{"body":"Built in maw workspace jarlcloth, commit 5d0ad21 (not live-tested). Core/Vadmal.cs: BoltCoins=10. Fine ruling pays the bot at once in undyed Homespun_WoolBolt into the treasury: thief's bag first, then stockpile bolts bought from the thief's hoard (10 coins each); remainder docked from wages as before. Trade: GoodsPrice prices bolts (wool 100 tenths, linen 80, dyed +50%); trader also packs stockpile bolts past 6 of each kind (Trade.BoltsForSale), counted in Lots."}	blake3:-3TYDudEsFa4ZRScN_jYJyFWnny0b4HJXbLMqhQtyM4
1792460472757860	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-14rw	{"body":"Decided (default, no layer slot): garments take the game's own slots (chest/legs/cape/utility). A layer slot is a new equipment slot that every client must sync, and it clashes with Quad's GearSlots rows. Garments earn their place by what they do (frost, rain, cold, comfort: Homespun 0.3.0) rather than armour. Bob can overrule."}	blake3:52ptj87HsbORFU-7qhLzFACPHrcZ7SkR4KAQhZR1Bf0
1792460472787394	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1xa6	{"body":"Homespun 0.3.0 (855c8ea). The cloak gives frost Resistant and the hood blocks rain Wet. Nalbinding blocks or removes Cold. Two dyed pieces give +1 comfort. All live-checked on Bob's character."}	blake3:IWVnrfIJrsdjgViQRQe9Vvv3yxfh97Xpg3Ov-lUW7zM
1792460472806392	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2pd8	{"body":"Nalbound mittens and socks added in Homespun 0.3.0 (sewing table: 6 yarn, utility slot). Recipe live-checked."}	blake3:6qfNVmrYxlOKp_-JJy6z13rNKPPgay9FEqY5cbNWIJw
1792460472826158	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-12o4	{"body":"Api v3 shipped in Homespun 0.3.0: ColourOf, Rgb, IsWarm, IsHooded, IsMittens, IsFine, IsWoolGarment, Sail, Sails, IsSail, StationsNear, Queue. Shipyard and Wayfinder use it."}	blake3:K8UYpdVwbkINvp6-W4KBNinrNuW4WEk4U-8E9Po128k
1792460472844678	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-610s	{"body":"Shipyard 0.3.2 (3c19e57): the knarr's mast stage takes a wool sail and shows the dye in its stripes, live-checked blue on the stocks. Wayfinder 0.1.12 (de4723d): a sail used on the helm rigs any ship, live-checked a karve set at half in yellow. Untested: a launched knarr's colour at sea, doing it by hand."}	blake3:eOkMMhGSribCmTSyMyiJYTo6t94BltlIemuss8-z09Y
