1792462526861104	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-7r9x	{"body":"2026-10-19, on Bob's character: holding the drop spindle spun 2 line flax into 4 linen thread within about a minute, without attacking. Pictures show a white whorl hanging below the right hand, but the hold pose isn't clear from the camera. Bob: check the pose by eye."}	blake3:C5r-cYpcbQg1TYifYkyK21tBbAo9tH1MyeAYJsrbk3c
1792462527044181	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2d24	{"description":"Seen 2026-10-19: weaver order #11 ('clothes') and later weave:ArmorDress4 stayed Open while Alfhild always took the priority-3 smelt orders for the retting pool, brake and wheel. Villagers in rags may never get sewn clothes; this could be why some have no tops. 0.1.221 gives only the ship's sail priority 4. Possible fix: raise clothes for the ragged above tending, or let the weaver take a craft order between station runs.","kind":"bug","labels":["jarldom","homespun"],"title":"Jarldom weaver: clothes orders (priority 2) starve behind station tending (priority 3)"}	blake3:2tT9ekLDkwkkGXgP2EzI0ow0DEF1h8tr0Xz6pivRetI
1792462810911413	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-233f	{"body":"Done 2026-10-19 (Jarldom 0.1.222). Tapestry feast on day 408: 2 tapestries hung, and the log has the hung-feast line. Vadmal: the bag route and the stores-with-hoard route both work, and the trader's bolts for sale and price are right. Test changes were undone. The wall hanging (test-tagged) stays in the great hall at 283.3,43.6,1123.2."}	blake3:lWfuphRMU1ELg1fOV1op-ei3U_OVu6SMjkzPrK-ASRo
1792462810930241	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-233f	{"state":"done"}	blake3:gcY020zBLadDG6Liol1RkaEL3hGhXszrORG1FRITDxs
1792463145138814	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3jul	{"body":"Done by hand on Bob's character, 2026-10-19 (Homespun 0.3.1). The vat's chest window opens (screenshot). Hover while steeping: 'Dyes 2 blue: steeping, 54s'. The bolts come out dyed once the vat is closed; the hover now says 'ready, close the vat' instead of 'steeping, 0s'. With blue bolts known, the sewing table offers Homespun_WoolTrousers_Blue and Homespun_Sail_Blue; other recipes stay hidden until their makings are known, as the game does. Colours: item renders look plain and lighter than Hildir's textured clothes, and lichen purple reads pinkish-magenta in bright light. Filed as a taste call for Bob."}	blake3:tijL1IUK8D8fkWmlo8HxhTq-KUMwY9FmuY9YCZiJFgs
1792463145157192	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3jul	{"state":"done"}	blake3:5Mz7CAyLQYFK417vain8QChEo_nUaSNMr1RzvBAizSI
1792463145276513	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2qzq	{"description":"From the 2026-10-19 render comparison (scratchpad tunics.png): dyed tunics are plain tints, lighter and flatter than Hildir's textured clothes. Lichen purple (0.40,0.20,0.44) reads pinkish-magenta when lit (real orchil is a red-purple, so it may be fine). Bob: deepen purple or add texture? Core/Dye.cs Colour.","kind":"task","labels":["homespun","needs-player"],"title":"Homespun dye colours: purple reads pinkish-magenta and dyed garments look flat next to Hildir's (taste call)"}	blake3:hlSVf4LbTKfkIXgcaaI3l_ILERxzQ5-qbNUe0oXK754
1792463902728961	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3rzp	{"body":"Live-tested 2026-10-19 on a private dedicated server (copy of Creative; Jarldom 0.1.222, Byre 0.2.0, Homespun 0.3.1) with Bob's game joined as a client. (1) Second client: the server-side villager Harald's purple tunic and blue trousers render in colour on the client (view shots). (2) Dropped item: client dropped Homespun_WoolTunic_Red; the server's colony hauler picked it up and holds it as Homespun_WoolTunic_Red (one prefab per colour, so the colour is the item's identity end to end). (3) Relog: fw back, fw go again; Harald still drawn with purple sleeves and blue trousers under his cape, and still carries the red tunic. Bob's bag compared exact afterwards; server stopped."}	blake3:GyTZsJVzhsHF22RNzQDOqDL1suBzaxfNqRsv95DqPhw
1792463902757488	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3rzp	{"state":"done"}	blake3:n-MgN88afgih8QxeCEusIInOf6KFHg5Blvrf0E5c6dQ
1792463912127104	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2dwf	{"description":"Seen 2026-10-19 on a private dedicated server (Creative copy, Jarldom 0.1.222): Bob's client dropped a test tunic at (290.8, 41.7, 1119.2) while standing at (289, 40.7, 1120), about 2 m away, and stayed there. Within about a minute Harald (hauler) had it in his bag. Villager/Work.cs's ground-haul scan skips drops with a player within 4 m (Player.GetAllPlayers), so either the scan runs where remote players aren't in that list, or the order was taken some other way. Cause not checked. Risk: on a server, a player's dropped things get carried off from under them.","kind":"bug","labels":["jarldom","needs-multiplayer"],"title":"Jarldom: hauler took a drop lying 2 m from a player on a dedicated server"}	blake3:9SrMGDJHWsMZrzdLaDcYErVxmJyFLuJsGxu9aVP8EFE
1792463920855364	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2kwh	{"description":"The spindle spins (live-checked 2026-10-19: 2 line flax to 4 linen thread in about a minute while held). What's left is taste: equip it and see whether the whorl hangs naturally below the right hand (equip offset -90 about x, as Godforged's hammer). Tune Things.cs's spindle offset if it looks off.","kind":"task","labels":["homespun","needs-player"],"title":"Homespun: drop spindle hold pose, check by eye"}	blake3:2T_YoahPAshu7yyioLLveJQR8WZlBtaP2OiZ63A4sGk
1792463920881961	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-7r9x	{"body":"Closing: the spindle and the wheel both work in play. The hold pose by eye is split off as a needs-player task."}	blake3:eb-QwKzE-2yR2P8NavUXhOK99NYehdekblltZJ4FL6c
1792463920902227	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-7r9x	{"state":"done"}	blake3:EVD0lA1ZBpDPJXRak-7XlMUD-f-FG3vPVoRsY5KYOf8
1792463920906520	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3kf	{"reason":"auto-completed: all children of bn-3kf are done","state":"done"}	blake3:Mwd3R73tQuSGwB7Z5xs9vr0j0gTYTEDuAzmB0Ek40AE
1792464718489066	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-383v	{"description":"bn-3tn9 ran 2026-10-19 before H2/H3: dyed prefabs, Jarldom colours/finery/vadmal/sail (0.1.216-0.1.222), Shipyard/Wayfinder sail binding were never run with Homespun or Jarldom swapped out. Rerun: GUID stub for Homespun (scratchpad hsafe/stub), then for Jarldom, on a throwaway character + world; check no exceptions, what drops, and that Bob's character never loads without the real mods. BLOCKED 2026-10-19: TrashPlanet won't load (see the cloud-index bone), and making a new world / repairing the cloud index was refused by auto mode, so Bob decides.","kind":"task","labels":["homespun","jarldom","save-safety","testing"],"parent":"bn-3kf","title":"Homespun: rerun the install/uninstall matrix on current builds (dyes, finery, sails, vadmal since bn-3tn9)"}	blake3:MDtoE-8Uc3rDssm7gQs6HqjZ5joIhAH9Mu4QGqQmgfA
1792464718619012	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-of6z	{"description":"After the bn-3tn9 test I restored worlds/TrashPlanet and characters/trash.fch by copying files on disk. Steam's remote storage still indexes the test's files (_main.12.*, 22_20__1_4.chunk: moved off disk to scratchpad hsafe/testsaves) and not the restored _main.9.* / 22_20__1_1.chunk, so the game says 'failed to load TrashPlanet: Connected Storage file missing'. trash.fch is indexed at 139480 bytes, the disk has the original 139154. Fix options for Bob: (a) let me write the originals back through SteamRemoteStorage.FileWrite and FileDelete the stale names (auto mode refused this); (b) put hsafe/testsaves back on disk (loads the post-test state); (c) restore TrashPlanet_backup_20261015-182532 via the game's Manage saves. Lesson: cloud saves are restored through the game/Steam API, never by copying files.","kind":"bug","labels":["needs-player"],"title":"TrashPlanet won't load: my file-copy restore desynced Steam's cloud index (2026-10-19)"}	blake3:e3KCqP1lieaRI4MC34rWdiFzgZ5e8H7Xi5CkfXsBnNs
1792464718647647	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3kf	{"body":"Closed by auto-completion of its children, but two acceptance criteria are not evidenced on current builds: 'no item loss in any install order' was tested (bn-3tn9) before dyes/H3/Jarldom's new Homespun code; 'each milestone useful alone' only by design (Api by reflection). Rerun filed as a child; blocked on Bob (TrashPlanet cloud index, new-world creation refused by auto mode). Evidenced: second-client dye check (bn-3rzp), weaver runs the chain (bn-31qi, bn-3vg1 live)."}	blake3:l9hdd_PEBo3ZLAvs9u5jnlyl_6FCkhROpOTbTnFw2xc
1792464830990922	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-383v	{"body":"Offline half done 2026-10-19 (current HEAD): code audit of every Jarldom call into Homespun (Compat/Compat.cs ApiRef binds by name+version; each wrapper returns null/empty/0 inside try/catch; every caller in Weaving, Dyeing, Tasks, Gear, Brain, Events vadmal, ColonyWindow, Actions is behind HomespunOn/HomespunDyeing or null-safe), Shipyard (Sailcloth.Sail null -> mast costs 15 DeerHide, tested 'Without Homespun: hides'), Wayfinder (Rigging.On false -> helm use falls through to the game). Homespun has no Jarldom reference. Tests: Homespun 234, Shipyard 65, Jarldom 3782 checks pass. Still needed live: Homespun stub and Jarldom stub loads (exceptions, what drops), blocked on bn-of6z / a throwaway world."}	blake3:d_6HQTWPE6QZEK-patHx4zhdfBt8tLwRvNNpDG24D7s
1792466021750411	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-383v	{"body":"Live rerun done 2026-10-19 on current builds (Homespun 0.3.2, Jarldom 0.1.222, Shipyard 0.3.3, Wayfinder 0.1.12), character 'trash' in a new local throwaway world HomespunTest (Bob: TrashPlanet was a throwaway). (1) Both: dyed cloak worn (frost Resistant), mittens, red sail, purple tunic, yellow bolt on the ground. (2) Homespun swapped for a GUID stub: its 4 bag items and the ground bolt dropped as the game does for any removed content mod (documented); every vanilla item and ground stack kept; no exceptions from Jarldom, Shipyard, Wayfinder or anything else. (3) Real Homespun back: works (cloak frost Resistant again). (4) Jarldom swapped for a GUID stub, Homespun kept: every Homespun item kept (red cloak worn and still Resistant, blue sail, yellow dress, mittens on the ground); only Jarldom's own Skald's drum dropped; no exceptions. (5) Both back: bag and ground identical to the Jarldom-less save. Stubs removed; real DLLs byte-checked in place."}	blake3:oR0nc6r2-ai8gw4P67OqR7uZSNKwsU2c_SCbImFWtGA
