1792523535301531	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3tne	{"body":"Measured 2026-10-20 with a scratchpad asset probe (counts by type+name, GC first), two hot reloads each. BuildShapes: nothing grows. Hallwright, Demolisher: their stake prefab holder, one a reload; fixed (old holder handed over via AppDomain data, destroyed once the new stake is registered): Demolisher 0.1.7, Hallwright 0.12.10, verified flat over 3 more reloads, stakes render. Factorheim: nothing on reload, BUT every world load rebuilt all 17 machines (+466 objects, ~37 icons) and kept the old set: fixed in 0.1.3 (unpublished, no dist). Same per-world-load leak in Homespun (piece icons, dye mesh+material), Shipyard (icons, water masks), Larder (station icons): new Looks.WorldOwned destroyed with the per-world prefabs; Homespun 0.3.3, Shipyard 0.3.4, Larder 0.1.1. Verified flat over two world loads, no broken renderers, Leftovers handover still frees."}	blake3:tvT8mDd_DXxzRq2zK6gxWyFZoD_2Jhg8jXNp0Cygb1I
1792523535321336	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-3tne	{"state":"done"}	blake3:23G_FWFHnw3h_yRuxB_unubcMIDh3Jadzj7q_yd5Uxk
1792523547367864	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3uwk	{"description":"Found 2026-10-20 while measuring bn-3tne. With a scratchpad probe (GC.Collect + Resources.UnloadUnusedAssets first), GC.GetTotalMemory after each logout + play Bob Creative: 1344 -> 1442; 1568 -> 1661 -> 1871 MB. Unity assets stay flat now (after Homespun 0.3.3, Shipyard 0.3.4, Larder 0.1.1, Factorheim 0.1.3), and hot reloads add only ~3 MB each, so it's the world load: something keeps the last world's managed objects alive (a mod's statics holding ZDOs/ZNetViews/lists, event handlers on game singletons) or the game itself. Next: compare with a vanilla-ish profile or bisect by mods (scripts folder), or a probe walking each loaded mod's static fields for collection sizes before/after a world load. Probe source: session a591fa09 scratchpad/assetprobe.","kind":"bug","labels":["perf"],"title":"Managed heap grows ~100-200 MB per world load (logout + play), not freed by GC"}	blake3:0Ueg5BMiKIpinsUZo-zU6ule_3Irx2EmAcanyMYnp-E
