1792530300173731	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-1tya	{"description":"# Context\nkit test (BuildKit 0.3.1) on 2026-10-20, pad at 400,1056 in Creative. A ridge vent stacked by its snap points on a grounded one: support 41 (both pitches) vs the game's wood_roof_top 84 / 79. Hung beside that one: 17 (26°) and 49 (45°) vs 100 / 60. In an earlier run the stacked vent fell outright. Every other kit piece matches its donor within a few points.\n# Likely cause\nKit.RidgeColliders replaces the ridge's boxes with two slope boards (lifted 0.02 m, 0.14 thick, from the slot's edge to the eave) and the hood's cap. Less collider meets a neighbour, so less support passes on.\n# Why it matters\nA vent far along a ridge from its walls may sag or break. It isn't seen in play yet: smoketest only set one on four poles.\n# Also seen (no change made)\nTurf roofs give a little less of the game's cover than the wooden roofs they're made from: about 0.35 vs 0.41-0.53 one tile overhead. It may matter for 'sheltered' in a big room. The numbers vary run to run by about ±0.06.\n# Acceptance\nkit test shows the ridge vents within about 10 points of wood_roof_top, stacked and beside; the smoke still goes out (kit smoketest).","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit","bug"],"size":"s","title":"BuildKit: ridge smoke vents pass on less support than the game's ridge (kit test finding)"}	blake3:qBVsPKZ4-Q_SZ9L4U8Oxe6YTyebikTkrdzs9IzJvIsg
1792531362266705	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2xcr	{"description":"# Seen 2026-10-20 in Creative (Golf 0.2.4, ClaudeTools golf shot), testing Jarldom's caddie\n- golf testcourse 12 at 386,1057.5 facing north, then golf starttest. First shot: golf shot putt 0.15 0 -1. The ball rolled about 4 m to 389.0, 31.74, 1054.0.\n- Every later shot (chip 0.45, putt 0.7, chip 0.5, aimed at the cup at 386.1,1069.5): strokes went up by one, impactSource 'animation', shotRejection empty, kinematic false. The ball stayed put, or moved back by up to 0.85 m.\n- The same after a relog, after testclear + a new testcourse (the ball returned to the new tee, same label, +1), with the caddie sent away, and with the player standing behind the ball.\n- The ball's y (31.74) is about 0.15 m under the ground height there (31.9). It may be lodged in the terrain after the first roll.\n# Not looked into further\nIt's Golf's own physics; the caddie only reads the Api. The closed practice ball is still at 385.0, 32.1, 1050.9. A Meadow golf club lies on the ground at about 385.5, 1049 (ClaudeTools clear 5 items didn't take it).","kind":"task","labels":["golf","bug"],"size":"s","title":"Golf: a ball stops responding to shots after its first (strokes count, the ball doesn't move)"}	blake3:Gl8TsNq9sd_YFvcjwWas0RyI5oCGtT9XBJoS0uMAWjU
1792531362321557	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-he3	{"state":"done"}	blake3:OZ5ISE0t6YiGQOLeCpE-8QVWOdZmTU8xMWJOsvMt7Zg
1792531380859663	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-he3	{"body":"Live-tested in Creative on a disposable test hole. Snjolaug followed as caddie ('caddying for Bob') and handed over the club with advice by the distance to the cup ('Here. Odin's watching.' at the tee, 'Chip it up close.' at 16 m, 'Read the slope. Then putt.' at 10 m). Shots that came no nearer got heckles ('No nearer than before, jarl.', 'A troll would have done better. Blindfolded.'). Fixed: the next hand-over now waits 4 s, so the verdict is heard. NOT seen: the cheer for a holed ball and the praise for a close shot, because Golf's ball stopped moving after its first shot (bug filed). The Golf entry in Jarldom's DESCRIPTION goes in its next release."}	blake3:e-E0D8hqnmUvT80pB8KHQpD035HwGRZLJrpQZcIh0YA
1792531452217114	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1mx	{"body":"Api design (2026-10-20, read from Quad's origin/main 04dbc26; nothing opened upstream yet, needs Bob's OK).\nBountyBoard keeps its State on the host (Posted/Active/Done Bounty lists, saved to DHack.BountyBoard.<worldUID>.txt). A Bounty is Kind Hunt|Elite|Sweep|Gather + Target + Count + Stars + Coins + Items, with Claimed and Earned player ids. Proposal: a host-only, polled BountyBoard.Api, Version 1.\n- string Post(string source, string kind, string target, int count, int stars, int coins, string title): kind 'hunt'|'elite'|'gather'. Adds an Active contract, with Source and Title as two NEW Bounty fields appended to Serialize (older versions read only the fields before them, as Earned already does). Returns its Id, or '' if not the host or the target isn't valid. Coins default 0: the poster pays its own way, so no double reward.\n- int StateOf(string id): 0 gone, 1 posted, 2 taken, 3 finished (waiting to be collected), 4 collected by everyone who earned it.\n- long[] EarnedBy(string id): who finished it.\n- bool Complete(string id, long player): finished from the other side (Jarldom's request handed in): Done, Earned += player.\n- bool Withdraw(string id): taken off the board (the request lapsed).\nThe window shows Title in place of the generated description when it's set.\nJarldom side (bn-2s4): post the requests that fit the board: a starred kill as Elite, a trophy or goods as Gather. A 'place seen' doesn't fit, so it isn't posted. Keep the contract id on the Request, and poll StateOf on the host every few seconds. Finished on the board: the request completes for EarnedBy[0]. Finished in Jarldom: Complete. Lapsed: Withdraw.\nPR: branch bob/bountyboard-api in ~/repos/valheim-mods, code + version bump + changelog + docs/bountyboard-api.md, no dist."}	blake3:fdUpI5hzQpq6azoIDXZBRcP_hM_OyDIYrzgGw7-DTDs
1792531698918800	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-20d0	{"state":"done"}	blake3:LvaIxGbJcRfbb5737blaP-frv4yRp1JKUHG6BnRpXKU
1792531699160007	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-u33n	{"description":"A client on a server with a different Mjölnir StrikeDamage (and GF_Mjolnir cost) should play with the server's values, and get its own back on leaving. Live-tested in single player only: the cost edit applied at once.","kind":"task","labels":["godforged","needs-multiplayer"],"size":"xs","title":"Godforged 0.3.3: check server-decided settings on a private dedicated server"}	blake3:9YIfhCwJQzjSyoE4lHNKCLhfUWs_5Dm42TyW-z2BaV0
1792533132529228	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3tvm	{"body":"Skíðblaðnir done in Godforged 0.3.4 (5b80636): the relic unfolds the game's karve by the water, a fair wind always behind her (patches Ship.GetSailForce/UpdateSail), and folds back only with her hold empty and nobody aboard. The relic and her ZDO share a token, because ZDO ids are renumbered each time the world loads. Live (Creative): unfolded, sailed dead into the wind at 6.3 m/s (the game's pull there is 0), 'moored 195 m away' from afar, refused to fold with Bob aboard, folded, left nothing behind. Remaining in this bone: Gleipnir's six-ingredient quest."}	blake3:zNqIflxeEmthPAg4WrW0PvwhMGz9YqMjG6WgJJGSU3c
1792533132802944	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2sdi	{"description":"Godforged 0.3.4's Skíðblaðnir always sails as if the wind were astern (a ZDO bool 'gf_skidbladnir' on her karve, FairWind server setting). Wayfinder's sail advice and HUD use the game's wind angle, so aboard her, heading upwind, it says 'headwind: row'. Read the ZDO flag (and Godforged's setting through an Api, or assume on) and give her full sail power in Policy.SailPower's callers.","kind":"task","labels":["wayfinder","godforged"],"title":"Wayfinder: know Skíðblaðnir's fair wind (HUD says 'headwind: row' aboard her)"}	blake3:ej59VDSes_VPCjTzSzsWHJKHmR39tEaDSGUPHUhKAAk
1792533133059354	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2o2k	{"description":"Tested with a test relic (gf skid), never from Bob's bag (it was full). Check: craft it at the forge (2), use it from the bag by the shore and at sea; put something in her hold and try to fold (should refuse: 'Empty Skíðblaðnir's hold'); a companion aboard should also block folding. Multiplayer: a client using the relic far from her asks the server (GF_SkidAsk/Tell); with Godforged missing on the server a client takes her as lost after 5 s. Hammer removal: no wood back (nobuildcost in Creative hides this anyway).","kind":"task","labels":["godforged","needs-player","needs-multiplayer"],"title":"Godforged Skíðblaðnir: player checks (bag use, a laden hold, multiplayer client)"}	blake3:sg9J38adtRj5LJjyEVDWJgpmPH946OwvW_bpEWLKbLU
1792533361788294	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2sdi	{"state":"done"}	blake3:3fwonj8zrbUSiiQ8WlpjgbgHa5UaJJm9hN0NXJonBUw
1792533900076426	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-2xcr	{"body":"Re-tested 2026-10-20 in Creative on the same spot (testcourse 12 at 386,1057.5, facing north). Not a Golf bug: the ground there is a sloped bowl.\n- The floor map shows 0.3–0.5 m dips at the 1 m scale, sloping down to the east and south.\n- A fresh ball rolled off the tee by itself, with 0 strokes, into the low spot at 389.43,31.75,1054.0.\n- Six shots in a row all moved it (5.6, 1.1, 2.9, 2.1 m and so on), but it rolls back down to around 390,1056 each time. Grass slows it by only 1.1 m/s², so it keeps rolling on any slope over about 6°.\n- 'y under the ground height' was GetGroundHeight against the collider: the floor there is 31.64, and the ball rests on it at 31.75 (radius 0.12).\n- My earlier 'stays put, or moves back up to 0.85 m' was the same roll-back.\nFor real courses: lay tees and cups on flatter ground, as players will. If Bob wants balls to hold on steeper greens, raise Rules.Resistance(Grass); that's a design call, not done.\nCleanup: the test tee and cup removed (testclear), the round stopped, the club dropped back where it lay (385.5,1049), and Bob's bag identical cell by cell."}	blake3:tJFHP6-yJpCJE_gsOKtNXW_PY7NGGsJSnBM41OI5r-M
1792533900105880	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-2xcr	{"state":"done"}	blake3:NEnIKaOy1LFMmRNA3XTjUVQ4np2AVSS_NDwxLfEkgBY
1792534211005355	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-1tya	{"body":"Fixed in BuildKit 0.3.2 (e99e158). Kit.RidgeColliders now keeps the game ridge's level beam box. That beam is what neighbours rest on: support points only count at or below the piece's centre of mass. Smoke balls ignore the beams of vents within 16 m when they're made (SmokeThrough, a postfix on Smoke.Awake). kit test at 400,1056: 26° stacked 75.6 / beside 52.2 (game 84.1 / 60.7); 45° 69.7 / 49 (game 78.9 / 59.8); before the fix it was 41 / 17–49. kit smoketest at 404,1062: about 7 of 12 balls near the vent were above the cap, rising to 47 m, so smoke still gets out. The rig was removed with greatwork rmpiece. Not done: the turf cover note (0.35 against the wooden roof's 0.41–0.53)."}	blake3:YJVPZaGTHzCkwkcPFdBGy0rFqrQdAteXSjZfKIMcGyk
1792534211058485	claude	itc:AQ		item.move	bn-1tya	{"state":"done"}	blake3:Mx323iZmmw-QMmU0orIBmJXrUavcTLuP8iNJFBs57qA
1792535404084899	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3uwk	{"body":"2026-10-20: added a static-field probe (scratchpad/staticprobe: StaticProbe.dll in scripts, loaded with 'reload StaticProbe'; it needs the dev loader, ScriptEngine refuses it at start without a pdb). It writes staticprobe-<tag>.txt when 'echo <tag> > BepInEx/claude/staticprobe.req' is run: after a full GC, every static and DontDestroyOnLoad collection's size and its destroyed Unity entries.\nResults over 2 world loads, then fixed:\n- Jarldom's instance-id caches piled up across worlds: Colony._names, Colony.Comps (+18k a load, dead Components), Classes._seats/_isTable, Work.FirstSeen, Passing.Done. They're now cleared on ZNet.Shutdown (Jarldom 0.1.228).\n- Byre Content.OurItems kept 7 dead prefabs a load (0.3.1).\n- Still growing, not ours: QualityOfLife ContainerRegistry.All, CraftFromChests/BuildFromChests ChestScanner.AllContainers and FeedFromChests ContainerRegistry.All gain 90 destroyed Containers a load. Filed for Quad as its own bone.\nThe heap still grows about 110-140 MB a load after a fresh restart (884, 1026, 1137 MB). None of the static collections holds that much, so the bulk is elsewhere: the game itself, Harmony or closure captures, instance events on per-scene singletons, or big arrays (vanilla Heightmap temp buffers are only ~100 KB). Next: a mono heap shot, or one world load with all mods but Jarldom/Gary/AICompanion moved out of scripts."}	blake3:IRVSH2G8mJ581Sc9x92UQMDE-3MByDAoyeCVYukaOuI
1792535404254167	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2roj	{"description":"Found 2026-10-20 with the static probe (bn-3uwk). Each world load (logout + play) adds about 90 entries to QualityOfLife.ContainerRegistry.All, CraftFromChests and BuildFromChests ChestScanner.AllContainers and FeedFromChests.ContainerRegistry.All, and every entry from past worlds is a destroyed Container (270/180 dead, then 360/270, then 450/360). Each keeps its managed Inventory alive and makes their scans walk dead entries. Fix upstream: drop nulls when scanning, or clear on ZNet.Shutdown. A PR to Quad's ~/repos needs Bob's OK first.","kind":"bug","labels":["perf","upstream"],"title":"Quad's chest mods keep destroyed Containers across world loads (QualityOfLife, CraftFromChests, BuildFromChests, FeedFromChests)"}	blake3:R0naoa69mossTlHI-dUHmF7AB4nrKuGY54MlpeG4wPI
1792535838638272	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3uwk	{"body":"Probe sources are now in the repo: tools/probes/staticprobe and tools/probes/assetprobe (see tools/probes/README.md), not the session scratchpad."}	blake3:GYwLXONRMXGpJAviUKQjkEqR03azDrXL39O5ws5H0hc
1792535838692712	claude	itc:AQ		item.comment	bn-3tvm	{"body":"Status: Draupnir, Brísingamen, Gjallarhorn (0.3.2) and Skíðblaðnir (0.3.4) are done. Only Gleipnir's six-ingredient quest is left. Template: Features/Gjallarhorn.cs or Skidbladnir.cs, registered in Core/Feature.cs Features.All; models in Models/*.py → json.gz; gameplay settings via Plugin.Synced.Bind; a gf test verb per feature."}	blake3:SBcm45oQ5CcPUF4BLbHofTgNT1jjxmrMH7Rwg7BvPSQ
1792535838880290	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-3rr5	{"description":"Seen in kit test 2026-10-20 (from bn-1tya, which is closed): one tile overhead, turf roofs give about 0.35 cover against their donors' 0.41-0.53, ±0.06 from run to run. It may matter for 'sheltered' in a big room. Measure with 'kit test <piece>' (its cover line) and compare Cover.GetCoverForPoint against the donor colliders. Not looked into.","kind":"task","labels":["buildkit"],"title":"BuildKit: turf roofs give less of the game's cover than the wooden roofs they're made from (~0.35 vs 0.41-0.53)"}	blake3:F0IGkAZeg5Bu-zVlmboywKiMq6_qvqUAxm_3-zNRXKc
1792535839129524	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2tcv	{"description":"From bn-2xcr (closed, not a bug): on a bowl-shaped test green every shot moved the ball, but it kept rolling back to the low spot. Rules.Resistance(Grass) is 1.1 m/s², so a still ball creeps on any slope over about 6°, and Roll only puts it to sleep under about 14°. Bob's call: leave it (realistic, so pick flat ground) or raise grass resistance or the sleep slope. Don't change it without his say.","kind":"task","labels":["golf","decision"],"title":"Golf: should balls hold on steeper greens? (grass resistance 1.1 m/s² rolls back on any slope over ~6°)"}	blake3:0-7gS3k-BNDwzyOkyDr6-dp874akjZYHkKv6tQSJRXY
1792535839334058	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-98r7	{"description":"Models/skidbladnir.py → skidbladnir.json.gz (0.3.4) uses the same colour-coded slots as the other Godforged relics (relics.py, gjallarhorn etc.), none of them baked. AGENTS.md and docs/model-baking.md want custom models baked onto a low-poly copy. Either bake the Godforged relic family together with a bake_conf.py, or get Bob to OK colour slots for small hand items. Its look: gf look GF_Skidbladnir.","kind":"task","labels":["godforged","models"],"title":"Godforged: Skíðblaðnir's relic model isn't baked (flat colour slots, ~2,200 tris)"}	blake3:hADYxJuuevcOwP4v9bljgd0eY3iQTUoG7OFxR7qn1vI
1792535839557342	claude	itc:AQ		item.create	bn-2izm	{"description":"Left in Bob's Creative world 2026-10-20:\n- A Meadow golf club (BobGolfClub) on the ground at about 385.5, 32.9, 1049.7. Claude Tools 'clear 5 items' didn't take it; 'pickup BobGolfClub' needs a free bag cell (Bob's bag is full: drop something first, as with Dandelion at [0,3]).\n- Bob's practice golf balls: each player keeps one ball that is reused. The closed one was at 385.0, 32.1, 1050.9. Harmless, but 'golf testclear' only removes markers.\n- Larder's test stations tagged larder_test by the knarr slipway, and a test churn, press and chest at 289-294.5, 1133.5. Remove with 'larder remove'; a chest with things in it is kept.\nLeave anything of Bob's alone. No Skíðblaðnir is left in the world ('gf skid ships' lists none).","kind":"task","labels":["cleanup"],"title":"Creative world test leftovers to clear (golf club, closed golf balls, Larder test stations)"}	blake3:NNlg5FS3_EeWj6YBlH7vIUmM2pEi-4snXor8GwPJdLI
